{
    "word": "hauberk",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "c9e188ba-a3b3-32b9-9041-239ef91a5125",
                "word": "hauberk",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c972e23b-f63a-4001-bca1-0271c4388943",
                        "entry_id": "c9e188ba-a3b3-32b9-9041-239ef91a5125",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "hauberks"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ac678032-5582-323e-8a9f-8b1dcca252f4",
                        "entry_id": "c9e188ba-a3b3-32b9-9041-239ef91a5125",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A coat of mail; especially, the long coat of mail of the European Middle Ages, as contrasted with the habergeon, which is shorter and sometimes sleeveless."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2cadab11-f40b-4ae0-8e65-092abf8f7f13",
                                "sense_id": "ac678032-5582-323e-8a9f-8b1dcca252f4",
                                "text": "The hauberk was a complete covering of mail from head to foot. It consisted of a hood, joined to a jacket with sleeves, breeches, stockings and shoes of double chain mail, to which were added gauntlets of the same construction."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "47cc2412-3fbf-419c-b8e7-698bad2358da",
                                "sense_id": "ac678032-5582-323e-8a9f-8b1dcca252f4",
                                "text": "Ursula wore that day a hauberk under her gown, and was helmed with a sallet; and because of her armour she rode upon a little horse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1d230dd-313d-46a6-94f8-4b5c1e1d3631",
                                "sense_id": "ac678032-5582-323e-8a9f-8b1dcca252f4",
                                "text": "The hauberk was to the Norman what the byrnie was to the Saxon, the chief method of bodily defence."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3e079368-5931-3162-b990-6fe6abd62920",
                        "entry_id": "c9e188ba-a3b3-32b9-9041-239ef91a5125",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A similar shirt of scale armour, plate, leather, or other armor material."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncommon"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa1c8325-3f8d-4453-befc-d6a3524a8f44",
                                "sense_id": "3e079368-5931-3162-b990-6fe6abd62920",
                                "text": "The habergeon is the mail in this case, and the hauberk is of plate or splint armour, while the cote-armoure is the surcoat, possibly thickly padded, as in the still-existing surcoat of the Black Prince."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd8e2f8e-eacc-4ef4-9dac-be9f9ad455a4",
                                "sense_id": "3e079368-5931-3162-b990-6fe6abd62920",
                                "text": "One, which was destined later to usurp the field completely, consisted of a sleeved mail or scale hauberk, probably of eastern, Iranian, origin, descending to the knees."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "460ecfaf-0944-4af8-8daf-952f641e9e85",
                                "sense_id": "3e079368-5931-3162-b990-6fe6abd62920",
                                "text": "In Demetrios ' portrait, the saint wears a lamellar hauberk and a long surcoat over ornately patterned leggings. The painter has added an unusual element to the composition - a scarf tied around the horse's head […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f3a1a8f3-75aa-4ac8-9cb2-3192fec0378e",
                                "sense_id": "3e079368-5931-3162-b990-6fe6abd62920",
                                "text": "Because the call to arms had come so quickly, he'd not had time to don his chain-mail armor, only a light, plate hauberk that covered his shoulders and torso."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4c430a63-e07e-4dde-88db-11ed5bab12d7",
                                "sense_id": "3e079368-5931-3162-b990-6fe6abd62920",
                                "text": "The plate hauberk did not restrict his movements in the slightest, and he didn't feel weighed down as he did in Taraq'nok's chain mail."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "51b1c3ec-742c-40c5-b7bc-2b20bf1b9eb0",
                                "sense_id": "3e079368-5931-3162-b990-6fe6abd62920",
                                "text": "Fitted perfectly for her, it consisted of a simple plate hauberk and legguards, plate armguards and sabatons with chain mail underneath. She had discarded the chain mail early, much to Parol's consternation, […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "279f6e0f-0be7-4911-9859-f51636b654ea",
                        "source_entry_id": "c9e188ba-a3b3-32b9-9041-239ef91a5125",
                        "source_sense_description": "A coat of mail",
                        "target_lang_word": "haubert",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "haubert",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1aa9eefa-f455-32bf-893f-9491120445d9",
                                        "entry_id": "7c4ae83e-b0a4-3045-9c06-9823e2467266",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sorte de cuirasse ancienne ou de cotte de mailles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Armurerie"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6f86982-bebc-4470-9573-b1dc9886e2de",
                                                "sense_id": "1aa9eefa-f455-32bf-893f-9491120445d9",
                                                "text": "En une heure de tête à tête public, dans un coin, sur un divan, la duchesse amena d’Esgrignon aux générosités scipionesques, aux dévouements amadisiens, aux abnégations du moyen âge qui commençait alors à montrer ses dagues, ses mâchicoulis, ses cottes, ses hauberts, ses souliers à la poulaine, et tout son romantique attirail de carton peint."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62188770-a6ae-4778-a298-092bd516f3d0",
                                                "sense_id": "1aa9eefa-f455-32bf-893f-9491120445d9",
                                                "text": "Un jeune homme… – traçons son portrait d’un seul trait de plume : — figurez-vous don Quichotte à dix-huit ans, don Quichotte décorcelé, sans haubert et sans cuissard, don Quichotte revêtu d’un pourpoint de laine dont la couleur bleue s’était transformée en une nuance insaisissable de lie-de-vin et d’azur céleste."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55dedee3-d744-46a1-80ea-1d8a529e3f0d",
                                                "sense_id": "1aa9eefa-f455-32bf-893f-9491120445d9",
                                                "text": "Cependant, réfléchis, noble Saxon, dit le chevalier ; tu n’as ni haubert, ni corselet, ni rien que ce léger heaume, un bouclier et une épée."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0eaabb1-709f-3817-9cfa-bb601e46ea4b",
                                        "entry_id": "7c4ae83e-b0a4-3045-9c06-9823e2467266",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fief de haubert : Fief dont le possesseur s'engageait à servir son suzerain contre le droit de porter une cotte de mailles. On dit aussi fief de haubergeon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c16db764-969d-415a-8da7-154814d12c06",
